A self-model assigns to each state an observer of the whole state space. The decisive operation asks each represented observer about its own state. Start with the visual story in the [Stanford Encyclopedia of Philosophy entry on self-reference](https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/self-reference/) and then experiment below.

## 1. Watch a fixed point become a loop

The diagonal construction turns completeness into a stable observation. A fixed observation remains fixed after every finite number of traversals.

