With $m$ states, the direct row-search takes $O(m^2)$ value comparisons. A matching row certifies a fixed point; a missing row explicitly certifies incompleteness for the transformed diagonal observer.

</details>

## 4. Learn an observer through its consequences

Every downstream probe $h:B\to X$ turns an observer $f:A\to B$ into $h\circ f$. The identity probe recovers $f$ itself, an elementary instance of the [Yoneda perspective](https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma).

